+# Reboot 27.11 local backend - candidate 1
+
+This ready-to-run Windows x64 package supplies the discovery access-token route
+and v2 discovery data missing from Reboot Launcher's older embedded backend.
+Those missing responses caused repeated HTTP 404s in the supplied 27.11 logs.
+It includes Node.js, installed dependencies, the original nonempty manifest and
+chunk files, and source code. No Node installation or compilation is required.
+
+This is a backend update. It does not establish that the experimental Erbium
+client/server DLLs are compatible or that the reported host crash is fixed.
+The latest client log showed a connection timeout after the host log stopped.
+
+## Start it
+
+1. Close the Fortnite host and playing client, then stop the embedded backend
+   using Reboot Launcher's Backend page.
+2. Extract the **entire** artifact ZIP into a writable folder such as
+   `C:\Reboot2711\Backend`. Run it from that folder, not from inside the ZIP.
+3. Double-click **START-BACKEND.cmd**. Keep its window open. It should report
+   `LawinServer started listening on port 3551` and an XMPP listener on port 80.
+4. In Reboot Launcher, open **Backend** and select type **Local**, port **3551**.
+   Use **Check server** if shown. The launcher should use the running backend.
+5. Keep the DLL selections below, then start the game-server instance and leave
+   it running. Start your separate playing client.
+6. For the first connection test, open the playing client's console with F8 or
+   tilde and enter `open 127.0.0.1:7777`.
+
+| Internal files setting | Selection |
+| --- | --- |
+| Authentication patcher | Existing Reboot-27.11-Auth.dll |
+| Unreal engine patcher | Existing Reboot-27.11-Client.dll |
+| Game server type | Custom |
+| Game server | Existing Reboot-27.11-Server.dll |
+
+The included backend listens only on this PC. HTTP uses 3551; XMPP/matchmaking
+uses 80. Port 8080 forwards to the local XMPP listener to support the cached
+configuration seen in the earlier logs. Game sessions point to 127.0.0.1:7777.
+The startup check reports occupied ports; it does not terminate other processes.
+
+Keep your old backend folder. This package has its own bundled profile/config
+files; it does not migrate custom edits or overwrite the old backend. It retains
+upstream's existing location for saved client settings. To return to the old
+backend, close this backend window and select Embedded in Reboot Launcher.
+
+## What was checked
+
+The Windows build verifies and includes the original manifest and chunk bytes,
+installs dependencies using the pinned package-lock.json, and tests the 27.11
+discovery-token response, v1/v2 discovery surfaces, default Solo playlist links,
+manifest HTTP body/hash, matchmaking destination, and both local WebSocket ports.
+It also checks that a second backend reports an occupied port instead of taking
+over the running one. See BUILD-INFO.txt for exact versions and workflow details.
+
+These are backend checks, not a full Fortnite match. A loading screen after a
+network timeout or a host crash still needs game/runtime investigation.
+
+If backend startup fails, read **backend-startup.log** beside START-BACKEND.cmd.
+For a game failure after switching, retain both game logs from the same attempt
+and any crash report produced by the game. Source and dependency licenses are
+included; no game binaries are bundled.
+
+## Provenance and changes
+
+LawinServer by Lawin0129 and contributors, GPL-3.0:
+https://github.com/Lawin0129/LawinServer/tree/7f0f26d7a772c6122c42b1783fd75f497e86d3a9
+
+The discovery fixes and payloads are provided by that upstream revision.
+This package adds the portable launcher, file/port checks, local-only listener
+configuration, an 8080-to-80 XMPP alias, and executable HTTP/WebSocket checks.
+It sets the STW event toggle to false to match the earlier launcher configuration.
+The backend HTTP port is fixed at 3551 for the existing authentication DLL.
+
+Unmodified official Node.js Windows x64 runtime, version 24.21.0:
+https://nodejs.org/dist/v24.21.0/
+
+The workflow verifies the Node ZIP using Node's published SHA256 list, retains
+its LICENSE in runtime/LICENSE, and records the archive/runtime hashes. The
+backend source, wrapper, tests, and npm dependency source are all included.
